From: pytorch-pyodide maintainers <noreply@github.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 17:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] Pass CMake project hooks before language setup

PyTorch's in-CMake environment forwarding runs after the top-level project()
command. Project hooks supplied only through that module therefore arrive too
late to affect the initial toolchain and language setup. Forward the two CMake
project hooks on the configure command line so they are active from the first
project() call.
---
 tools/setup_helpers/cmake.py | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tools/setup_helpers/cmake.py b/tools/setup_helpers/cmake.py
--- a/tools/setup_helpers/cmake.py
+++ b/tools/setup_helpers/cmake.py
@@ -287,6 +287,16 @@ class CMake:
             "BUILD_TEST": build_test,
         }
 
+        # EnvVarForwarding.cmake runs after the top-level project() command,
+        # but these hooks must be defined before that command starts toolchain
+        # and language initialization. Keep other CMAKE_* forwarding in CMake.
+        for project_hook in (
+            "CMAKE_PROJECT_INCLUDE_BEFORE",
+            "CMAKE_PROJECT_INCLUDE",
+        ):
+            if project_hook_value := my_env.get(project_hook):
+                build_options[project_hook] = project_hook_value
+
         # FindPython cannot infer target headers from the host interpreter
         # while cross-compiling. Pyodide supplies the target include directory
         # explicitly so CMake keeps BUILD_PYTHON enabled and creates torch._C.
-- 
